Wait, I just gave your example a more thorough read-through. Seems like you might just want to put the if/else statement outside of the grouping call?

group_by_switch <- function(data, switch){
  if (switch == T) {
    data <- data %>%
      group_by(carb)
  } else {
    data <- data %>%
      group_by(am)
  }
}

mtcars %>%
  group_by_switch(switch = T) %>%
  tally()

mtcars %>%
  group_by_switch(switch = F) %>%
  tally()

Michael Culshaw-Maurer
Grad Group in Ecology
Rosenheim/Schreiber Labs
Briggs 320

