Also check out RSpatial.org which Robert Hijmans and his lab writes and maintains.  It’s pretty similar to what he teaches, I believe, so you can get a preview of the potential concepts.  For basic R, check out the Data Carpentry ecology lessons and there’s a whole Geospatial workshop which is still in development, but has different material than Robert’s site.

Michele

