Hi folks,

Late notice (apologies!) but we are having a presentation currently by Alicja Gosiewska on using XAI (see below!). She's visiting from Poland and we are happy to have her present today! Alicja Gosiewska (https://github.com/agosiewska) is a Ph.D. student at Warsaw University of Technology in Poland, currently visiting The Genome and Biomedical Sciences Facility.

"I work in the MI2 Data Lab group (http://mi2.mini.pw.edu.pl/) where currently we are focusing on the field of Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI). Our research aims to develop methods that help to understand how complex machine learning models work and to increase the trust in their predictions. An overview of our work can be found at http://jmlr.org/papers/v19/18-416.html. We also develop many R packages for XAI (http://drwhy.ai)."

Zoom link for presentation is here:

https://zoom.us/j/375570526

Notes/slides/materials:
https://github.com/agosiewska/XAI-UC-Davis

